2026-08-12T15:10:16.870165Z  WARN rs_cam_gui: MCP mode on Wayland. This launch requests PresentMode::AutoNoVsync, which on a surface offering Mailbox or Immediate removes the measured park: a minimised window kept painting and every MCP call answered live. CHECK WHICH MODE YOU GOT — `generation_status` reports it as `frame_loop.present_mode.negotiated`, and the startup log prints it. If it says Fifo or FifoRelaxed, the hazard is back: a hidden, occluded or screen-locked window can block the main thread inside the present, and every MCP request plus every generate_all round handoff stalls indefinitely with the compute lane reporting idle (`frame_loop.healthy: false`). The certain remedy is still to relaunch with WAYLAND_DISPLAY unset so winit picks X11/XWayland, where a window that stops painting does not strand dispatch. Setting WINIT_UNIX_BACKEND does NOT work — winit removed that variable in 0.29 and this build is on 0.30. Coverage caveat: the flip is measured against a MINIMISED window; occluded and visible-but-frozen states are not yet measured (pending N-3).
